2. Essential Ingredients of Criminal Breach of Trust (Section 405 IPC): To constitute criminal breach of trust, two basic requirements must be established:
(1) Entrustment of property or with any dominion over property;
(2) Dishonest misappropriation, conversion to one's own use, or dishonest use or disposal of that property in violation of any direction of law or legal contract prescribing the mode in which the trust is to be discharged.
